;; rules/booklogic/predicates.edn — predicate signatures for this verifier.
;;
;; FORM SYNTAX:
;;   (defpredicate :predicate-name [:arg-sort-1 :arg-sort-2 ...] :return-sort)
;;
;; Valid sorts: anything declared in sorts.edn OR the primitive set
;;   {:int :real :bool :string :entity :formula}
;;
;; EXAMPLE (commented out — uncomment and edit for your domain):
;; (defpredicate :osmotic-pressure-pa [:solution] :real)
;; (defpredicate :molarity            [:solution] :real)
;; (defpredicate :vant-hoff-i         [:solution] :real)
;; (defpredicate :temperature-k       [:solution] :real)
;;
;; COMMON SILENT FAILURES:
;;   - declaring :return :int when the regex extracts "2.5" → the lift coerces
;;     to int(0) silently. Pick :real for any predicate whose canonical text
;;     may contain a decimal point.
;;   - uppercase letters in the predicate name (`:Osmotic-Pressure`) → all
;;     claims for that predicate fall through to OPAQUE; Phase A's
;;     extract gate (`make extract`) surfaces this as "OPAQUE fraction exceeds
;;     threshold". Use kebab-case for predicate names.
;;   - missing :arg-sorts vector entirely → nbb throws at compile time.
;;
{:forms
 [(defpredicate :basic-reproduction-number [:disease]    :real)
  (defpredicate :vaccination-coverage      [:population] :real)
  (defpredicate :herd-immunity-threshold   [:disease]    :real)]}
